{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 19, :comments ["<b>For the man is a tree of the field.</b> Ki serves like ela, meaning: rather, a tree in which a man can come at you in the siege — for example, if there is a forest growing and producing fruit before the city, and a man can enter there and hide and lie in wait for you and come at you in the siege with which you are surrounding it — you may destroy it. Another interpretation: invert the verse and expound it, and this is what it says: ואותו לא תכרות וגו׳ — לבא מפניך במצור, meaning, to make from it a siege-engine to conquer the city. כי האדם עץ השדה — לאכלה, ולא תשחיתהו."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 20, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:01:07.791488657Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}